Subject: add virtual vias in a stable order; hash joints by position only
Upstream-file: pcbnew/router/pns_joint.h (JOINT_TAG_HASH), pcbnew/router/pns_node.cpp (NODE::FixupVirtualVias)
Why: JOINT_TAG_HASH mixed the net's POINTER into the hash, so NODE::m_joints
 (an unordered_multimap) iterated in an order that moved with ASLR, and it
 differs between standard libraries in any case. FixupVirtualVias walks
 m_joints and Adds a virtual via per qualifying joint in that order; with
 patch 0003 an item's serial is its order as an obstacle, so two equally near
 virtual vias were still ordered by address, one map over from the one 0003
 fixed (review r3 D-1; latent: no golden line or fixture route has two tied).
 The virtual vias are now sorted by (position, layer, diameter) before they
 are added, and the hash uses the position only (equality still compares the
 net). The residue: two virtual vias of two different nets at one position,
 layer and diameter (a short) keep the table's order.
Upstream: yes, as a determinism fix with 0003; not yet proposed.

--- a/pcbnew/router/pns_joint.h
+++ b/pcbnew/router/pns_joint.h
